ECS + ALB + Auto Scaling Lab

>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Create ECS Cluster

Fargate
harish-httpd-cluster

>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Create Task Definition

Image: httpd:latest
Port: 80
CPU: 0.25 vCPU
Memory: 0.5 GB

>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Create ALB

Internet-facing
Listener: HTTP:80
Security Group: allow 80

>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Create Target Group

Target type: IP because we're using Fargate
Protocol: HTTP
Port: 80
Health check: /

>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Create ECS Service

Service: httpd-alb-service
Fargate
Connect existing ALB
Connect target group

>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Verify

ECS Task → RUNNING
Target Group → Healthy
Open ALB DNS → Apache “It works!”

<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<Manual Scaling

Plain Text
Desired tasks: 1 → 3

ECS created multiple Fargate tasks.

>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Auto Scaling

Plain Text
Minimum: 1
Maximum: 4
CPU target: 50%
Policy: httpd-cpu-autoscaling
Architecture

Internet → ALB → Target Group → ECS Service → Fargate Tasks

>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>Important troubleshooting

If target is Unhealthy / Request timed out:

Check container port 80
Check ECS task Security Group
Allow port 80 from the ALB Security Group
For Fargate, Target Group type should be IP
Check health path /
